name: sim.getObjectOrientation
description: Retrieves the orientation (Euler angles) of an object
luaSynopsis: list eulerAngles = sim.getObjectOrientation(int objectHandle, int relativeToObjectHandle = sim.handle_world)
pythonSynopsis: float[3] eulerAngles = sim.getObjectOrientation(int objectHandle, int relativeToObjectHandle = sim.handle_world)
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object. Can be combined with sim.handleflag_reljointbaseframe (see next argument)
2. relativeToObjectHandle: indicates relative to which reference frame we want the orientation. Specify sim.handle_world to retrieve the absolute orientation, sim.handle_parent to retrieve the orientation relative to the object's parent, or an object handle relative to whose reference frame you want the orientation. If this handle is the handle of a joint, then the orientation relative to the joint's moving frame will be returned (unless objectHandle is combined with sim.handleflag_reljointbaseframe, in which case the orientation relative to the joint's base frame will be returned).
outputs:
1. eulerAngles: Euler angles [alpha beta gamma]
replacedBy:
- name: getQuaternion, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_getQuaternion.method
- name: quaternion, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_quaternion.property
- name: worldQuaternion, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_worldQuaternion.property
- name: eulerAngles, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_eulerAngles.property
- name: worldEulerAngles, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_worldEulerAngles.property
